{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"REBAR-DEBUG PHASE 1 — mechanism confirmed; design-gated, no repair applied\n\nConfirmed mechanism: an accepted forced-review request has no durable identity. `/rerun` resets its retry budget, places the sole `_rebar_force` event on the process-local asyncio queue, and returns 202. Accepted `recheck-review` likewise resets the budget, posts an affirmative queued reply, and only then returns a forced event that the worker requeues. The SQLite store contains only `voted` and `review_attempts`; after process loss, `reconcile_once` sees only an ordinary patchset event and skips it when Gerrit already has a vote.\n\nRuntime proof: a real `/rerun` request returned 202 with `{queued:true,force:true}` and queue depth 1; after simulated restart the fresh queue was empty, the durable tables had no pending-force row, and real reconciliation of the same already-voted revision scanned 1/reviewed 0. Controls passed: a vote-less revision is reviewed by reconciliation, and direct `review_and_vote(force=True)` bypasses both vote guards and re-votes while force=False skips. Routine graceful shutdown may drain fast work; the proven loss window is hard death or the bounded drain/cancel window expiring.\n\nClassification under the original-intent guard: `cannot-determine` / design decision required. ADR 0009 §7a, the runbook, and review policy promise an operator/contributor escape hatch that enqueues and re-reviews a stuck vote, which supports durability. But the original S4b story and ADR explicitly define the durable reconciler only for vote-less patchsets, the contributor story requires reset+enqueue+reply without persistence, and the introducing design chose an in-memory queue. No original epic explicitly requires an accepted forced request to survive restart. Adding `forced_pending` therefore creates retry/coalescing semantics rather than restoring an unambiguous documented contract.\n\nDecision needed before Phase 2: should accepted `/rerun` and `recheck-review` requests be at-least-once durable across process loss? If yes, the design must define request generations/coalescing (avoiding an ABA clear), persist before budget reset/public acknowledgement, define stale requests after new revisions/closure, and clear only the matching successful forced review. No code changed."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786302704798575001,"uuid":"3048c5e2-0654-4483-b427-c898ef10ae44"}